Subject: [PATCH] content: Web Share follows the claimed platform, not the build

navigator.share/canShare are compiled in on every platform, but chrome/
only enables the WebShare runtime feature on Android, ChromeOS, Windows
and macOS (chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc,
SetRuntimeFeaturesDefaultsBeforeBlinkInitialization: "to avoid it being
made available in WebView or Linux"). A Linux build with a profile
claiming Windows or macOS is therefore missing an interface the claimed
device has, which the V3 prototype.shape probe reports.

Same shape as patch 0025 for WebBluetooth: no json5 flip is needed
because WebShare ships as status "test" and is reachable through
EnableFeatureFromString. This decides it from the profile's claimed
platform in SetCustomizedRuntimeFeaturesFromCombinedArgs. With no profile
loaded nothing is touched and the build behaves as upstream says.

Only API presence follows the profile. canShare() evaluates its
arguments locally in Blink; share() still goes through the platform
ShareService, which has no Linux implementation, so invoking it on Linux
rejects exactly as a stock Linux build with the feature forced on would.
Nothing is spoofed: the capability the reference exposes is the API the
reference ships.

Ledger: api.webshare-presence.
diff --git a/content/child/runtime_features.cc b/content/child/runtime_features.cc
--- a/content/child/runtime_features.cc
+++ b/content/child/runtime_features.cc
@@ -496,6 +496,31 @@ void SetCustomizedRuntimeFeaturesFromCombinedArgs(
     }
   }
 
+  // Web Share follows the platform the profile claims, not the platform we
+  // built for. Same shape as the WebBluetooth block above (patch 0025).
+  //
+  // navigator.share/canShare are compiled in everywhere, but chrome/ enables
+  // the WebShare runtime feature only on Android, ChromeOS, Windows and macOS
+  // (chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc: "to avoid it being
+  // made available in WebView or Linux"). A profile claiming Windows or macOS
+  // would otherwise be missing an interface the claimed device has.
+  //
+  // No json5 flip is needed: WebShare ships as status "test", reachable via
+  // EnableFeatureFromString, and this decides it from the claimed platform.
+  // With no profile loaded nothing is touched.
+  {
+    bool share = false;
+    if (const base::apostate::Profile* profile =
+            base::apostate::Profile::Get()) {
+      if (const std::optional<std::string>& claimed = profile->ua_platform()) {
+        share = (*claimed == "Windows" || *claimed == "macOS");
+      }
+    }
+    if (share) {
+      blink::WebRuntimeFeatures::EnableFeatureFromString("WebShare", true);
+    }
+  }
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   if (base::android::android_info::sdk_int() <
       base::android::android_info::SDK_VERSION_P) {
